language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ big_bang2: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Nontransitive dice: find a set of five dice such that the dominance relationships between the dice are isomorphic to those of Rock-Paper-Scissors extended by Lizard and Spock. Rock (1) crushes Scissors (3) and crushes Lizard (4); Paper (2) covers Rock (1) and disproves Spock (5); Scissors (3) cuts Paper (2) and decapitates Lizard (4); Lizard (4) eats Paper (2) and poisons Spock (5); Spock (5) vaporizes Rock (1) and smashes Scissors (3). Each die has six faces, each face value is an integer from 1 to 12, and faces may repeat. A die A beats a die B when A has a strictly larger face value than B in more than half of all the pairs of faces (one face of A with one face of B).
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/big_bang2.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ the number of faces on each die, and how many of the face pairs one die must win to beat another
letting faces = 6
letting majority = 19
$ dice[d,p]: face p of die d, where die 1 is Rock, 2 Paper, 3 Scissors, 4 Lizard and 5 Spock, indices 1-based
find dice : matrix indexed by [int(1..5), int(1..faces)] of int(1..12)

such that
$ symmetry breaking: the faces of a die can be listed in any order, so the faces of each die are listed in increasing order
forAll d : int(1..5) . forAll p : int(1..faces-1) . dice[d,p] <= dice[d,p+1],
$ Rock beats Scissors: Rock has the larger face in more than half of the 36 face pairs (at least 19)
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[1,p] > dice[3,q]))) >= majority,
$ Rock beats Lizard
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[1,p] > dice[4,q]))) >= majority,
$ Paper beats Rock
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[2,p] > dice[1,q]))) >= majority,
$ Paper beats Spock
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[2,p] > dice[5,q]))) >= majority,
$ Scissors beats Paper
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[3,p] > dice[2,q]))) >= majority,
$ Scissors beats Lizard
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[3,p] > dice[4,q]))) >= majority,
$ Lizard beats Paper
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[4,p] > dice[2,q]))) >= majority,
$ Lizard beats Spock
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[4,p] > dice[5,q]))) >= majority,
$ Spock beats Rock
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[5,p] > dice[1,q]))) >= majority,
$ Spock beats Scissors
(sum p : int(1..faces) . (sum q : int(1..faces) . toInt(dice[5,p] > dice[3,q]))) >= majority
